{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review follow-up for the pi backend you wrote (PR #32). Branch `16-pi` has since been rebased onto origin/main and has two extra commits (pi fixture test: CANCELLED assertion dropped, generic `lane-*` arm). Start from the current HEAD; don't undo them. Do not delegate further.\n\nRequired:\n1. tests/live.rs: add a second `#[ignore = \"needs a logged-in pi; spends one muse-spark request\"]` test. It runs `scripts/record.sh pi opencode-go/muse-spark-1.3-contributor read-write live-plain-answer <tmpdir>` with the prompt \"What is 17 * 23? Answer with just the number.\" on stdin. That records a fresh redacted fixture, `tests/fixtures/pi/live-plain-answer.stdout`. Init the tmpdir as a git repo first if record.sh or pi needs one. The test then parses the fixture with `delegate::backends::pi::parse_stdout` and asserts the text contains 391, a session id is present, and cost_usd > 0. Do NOT run it, and do NOT commit any fixture.\n2. Session fallback: when the stream has no `session` header, `BackendResult.session_id` must be the `--session-id` the run was launched with. In `spawn`, take that value from `spec.argv` and pass it to `finish` as the fallback. Add a unit test that strips the header from plain-answer and checks the fallback.\n3. `agent_end` with no assistant message: `is_error: Some(true)`, text \"no result line\". Add a unit test.\n\nCut-only (apply each only if it removes lines and keeps every test green; otherwise skip it and say so):\n4. A `num(usage, key)` helper for the repeated usage-field chain in `handle_line`.\n5. Remove the redundant `.is_none()` early return near line 145.\n6. pi doctor: drop the duplicate `report.warnings.push` on auth failure if `lines()` already emits that warning from `model_failures` (doctor output must not change).\n7. Share `command_err` between the cursor and pi doctors.\n8. Replace pi doctor's `empty_report()` with `#[derive(Default)]` on `DoctorReport` (or `impl Default`).\n9. One `reject_pi_read_only(..)` helper used by both `run` and `resume` in src/cli.rs.\n\nThen `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo test` must pass. Make a new commit (no amend) ending `Co-Authored-By: Muse Spark <noreply@opencode.ai>`. Do not push. Report: the commit SHA, which cut-only items you applied or skipped and why, the test summary. Then Friction: up to 3 bullets.\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}],"timestamp":1790856579334}}
