d`), budgets 6, cli_e2e 27, cli_info_e2e 6, pi_e2e 6, live 2 ignored (pre-existing cursor + new pi, never run, no fixture written) — 187 passed, 0 failed. Note: the `cancelled` assertion now expects the header session id, since a header-less-or-not result carries the launch id — which also makes resume-after-cancel possible for pi.\n\nFriction:\n- `budgets` doctor timing flaked once under parallel test-binary load (pass solo, pass on full re-run); that suite's serial-mutex only covers its own binary.\n- One overlapping multi-edit duplicated a `spawn` block; caught by reading the file back before building.\n- The live test shells `git init` unconditionally rather than only-if-needed, since whether pi wants a repo is unknown — harmless, but slightly stronger than the brief's conditional.\n\nSTATUS: DONE","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_01a0f7633c1a767d92c8fa47169f6a9d\"}"}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"opencode-go","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","usage":{"input":533,"output":707,"cacheRead":194673,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":299,"totalTokens":195913,"cost":{"input":0.0000533,"output":0.00014140000000000002,"cacheRead":0.00038934600000000005,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0005840460000000001}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1790856862470,"responseId":"resp_6abe4ea34d0df44185ca49d3","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"high"}],"willRetry":false}
